x86_64-linux  the constructors and destructors of A, B and D are implicit, so clang writes only the form a use asks for and cxx1 writes both of Itanium's - see docs/CONFORMANCE.md, "An inline member function is a strong symbol". The names this case exists to check agree exactly: _ZN1D2fbEv, and the thunk _ZThn8_N1D2fbEv that the secondary table points at, which is the whole question
arm64-darwin  same, and narrower: only A's and B's implicit C1 constructors, which are never called here as complete objects because both are built as bases of D. Every other name agrees, the thunk included
